This is a human-readable summary of (and not a substitute for) the license.

You are free to:

  - Share — copy and redistribute the material in any medium or format
  - Adapt — remix, transform, and build upon the material

Under the following terms:

  - Attribution — You must give appropriate credit, provide a link to the
    license, and indicate if changes were made. You may do so in any
    reasonable manner, but not in any way that suggests the licensor
    endorses you or your use.

  - NonCapitalist — You may exercise the rights granted only if you are a
    worker-owned business, a worker-owned collective, a non-profit
    organisation, or an individual person. All financial gain, surplus,
    profits and benefits produced by the business or collective using the
    licensed material shall be distributed among the workers and collective
    owners. Any use by a for-profit entity owned or controlled by capital,
    or any use where the surplus value produced is appropriated by owners
    who are not the workers, is NOT permitted under this license and
    requires a separate commercial agreement with the licensor.

  - ShareAlike — If you remix, transform, or build upon the material, you
    must distribute your contributions under the same license as the
    original.

  - No additional restrictions — You may not apply legal terms or
    technological measures that legally restrict others from doing anything
    the license permits.

================================================================================
PEER PRODUCTION LICENSE — FULL TEXT
================================================================================

The Peer Production License is a "copyfarleft" license: it permits commons-based
peer producers, worker-owned cooperatives, and non-profit organisations to use,
copy and adapt the licensed work, including for monetary compensation, while
denying that permission to capitalist enterprises that would extract surplus
value from the labour of others.

Section 1 — Definitions.

  a. "Licensed Material" means the artistic, documentary, software or other
     work to which the licensor applied this license.

  b. "You" means the individual or entity exercising the rights granted by
     this license.

  c. "Collective" means a worker-owned business or worker-owned collective in
     which all surplus is distributed to its worker-members; a non-profit
     organisation; or an individual natural person acting in their own name.

  d. "Adapted Material" means material derived from or based upon the Licensed
     Material.

Section 2 — Scope.

  a. License grant. Subject to the terms of this license, the licensor grants
     You a worldwide, royalty-free, non-sublicensable, non-exclusive license
     to exercise the rights in the Licensed Material to reproduce, adapt and
     share the Licensed Material, in whole or in part.

  b. Permitted commercial use. You may exercise the rights granted herein for
     commercial purposes ONLY if You are a Collective as defined in Section 1(c)
     and any surplus produced is shared among the worker-members. Use of the
     Licensed Material by an enterprise whose surplus is appropriated by
     non-working owners or shareholders is NOT permitted under this license.

  c. Non-permitted use. Any commercial use that does not satisfy Section 2(b)
     requires a separate written agreement with the licensor, actitude.org.

Section 3 — License Conditions.

  a. Attribution. If You share the Licensed Material or Adapted Material, You
     must retain identification of the creator (actitude.org), a copyright
     notice, a reference to this license, a disclaimer of warranties, and a
     URI or hyperlink to the Licensed Material where reasonably practicable.

  b. ShareAlike. If You share Adapted Material, the license You apply to it
     must be this Peer Production License or a later version thereof.

  c. No additional restrictions. You may not offer or impose any additional
     or different terms, or apply any technological measures, that restrict
     exercise of the rights granted under this license.

Section 4 — Disclaimer of Warranties and Limitation of Liability.

  The Licensed Material is offered "as-is" and "as-available". The licensor
  makes no representations or warranties of any kind concerning the Licensed
  Material. To the extent possible, the licensor shall not be liable to You
  on any legal theory for any losses, costs, expenses or damages arising out
  of the use of the Licensed Material.

Section 5 — Term and Termination.

  This license applies for the term of the copyright in the Licensed Material.
  If You fail to comply with this license, then Your rights under it terminate
  automatically.

